2. PROJECT TITLE

Personal Portfolio Website


3. OBJECTIVE

The objective of this project is to create a responsive personal
portfolio website using HTML, CSS and JavaScript.

The website showcases my personal information, technical skills,
projects and contact details.


4. TEMPLATE / STARTING POINT

The portfolio website was created from scratch using HTML, CSS
and JavaScript.

AI assistance was used for generating the initial structure,
improving the design and simplifying parts of the code.


5. AI TOOLS USED

Tool Used: ChatGPT, Claude

I used ChatGPT for:

• Modify the initial HTML structure
• Making the website responsive
• Improving the portfolio design
• Troubleshooting and modifying the code

I used Claude for:
• Make attractive design in CSS file
• Portfolio design reference
• Make my project somewhere errorless

6. PROMPTS USED

Some of the prompts used while creating the website were:

1. "Help me with HTML, CSS and JS file."

2. "Make it attractive set a nice background."

3. "In this CSS file set the background with some tech
    and programming theme."

4. "Drowsiness project and make a place for it."


7. METHOD / APPROACH

Step 1:
Created the basic HTML structure of the portfolio.

Step 2:
Added Home, About Me, Skills, Projects and Contact sections.

Step 3:
Created CSS styling for the website.

Step 4:
Added a dark technology-themed background and responsive design.

Step 5:
Used JavaScript for the mobile navigation menu and contact form.

Step 6:
Added my Calculator, To-Do List, Drowsiness Detection and
Personal Portfolio projects.

Step 7:
Uploaded the project files to GitHub.

Step 8:
Hosted the portfolio website using GitHub Pages.

Step 9:
Added a Download Documentation button to the footer.


